<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:54:36 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>International</category><title>Belgium turns to European air support as wildfire rages near German border</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260816-belgium-turns-to-european-air-support-as-wildfire-rages-near-german-border</link><description>
Belgium called in aerial reinforcements from across Europe on Sunday as firefighters battled the country’s largest wildfire in more than a century, with flames spreading rapidly through a difficult-to-reach nature reserve near the German border.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/baaa53f4-996b-11f1-ba0b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Belgium-Wildfire.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/baaa53f4-996b-11f1-ba0b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Belgium-Wildfire.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cdccd256-9955-11f1-9ad6-2b9ea6a90619</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:24:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/baaa53f4-996b-11f1-ba0b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Belgium-Wildfire.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's successive heatwaves show strain of living in urban 'heat islands'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260815-france-s-successive-heatwaves-highlight-strain-of-living-in-urban-heat-islands</link><description>
As France experiences its latest heatwave, residents of urban "heat islands" – dense neighbourhoods with few trees or green spaces – are suffering acutely in the high temperatures, and local authorities are searching for solutions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0ac01ac-5275-11f0-b313-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/36a61f85-934d-4cd7-acd5-e4137a8ee89a.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0ac01ac-5275-11f0-b313-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/36a61f85-934d-4cd7-acd5-e4137a8ee89a.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e08ea958-97db-11f1-ac97-c132d391fb73</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 10:43:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0ac01ac-5275-11f0-b313-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/36a61f85-934d-4cd7-acd5-e4137a8ee89a.jpeg">© Théo Renaudon/RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>Europe's shrinking rivers give rise to debate over how to tackle drought</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260816-europe-s-shrinking-rivers-give-rise-to-debate-over-how-to-tackle-drought</link><description>
Europe's shrinking rivers are disrupting industry, reducing power generation and intensifying the debate over how to respond to worsening drought. As water levels fall across the continent, authorities and businesses alike are looking for ways to keep freight moving and critical infrastructure operating. Hydrologists warn, however, that digging rivers deeper cannot create more water and could make shortages worse.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/501dd132-9056-11f1-aee0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26209461327444.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/501dd132-9056-11f1-aee0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26209461327444.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6b280094-97ca-11f1-90af-371e64013e18</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 07:17:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/501dd132-9056-11f1-aee0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26209461327444.jpg">© Federico Gambarini/DPA via AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Solar-powered community gardens offer lifeline in drought-hit Zimbabwe</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260816-solar-powered-community-gardens-offer-lifeline-in-drought-hit-zimbabwe</link><description>
At a shared garden in eastern Zimbabwe, solar-powered pumps are helping farmers grow crops year round, even when drought dries out other fields. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81a7bf68-97c4-11f1-a9f5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Berita-Numbi-in-Mutekwatekwa-community-garden-in-Mutare-RFI-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81a7bf68-97c4-11f1-a9f5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Berita-Numbi-in-Mutekwatekwa-community-garden-in-Mutare-RFI-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d9d4442e-97c7-11f1-a081-371e64013e18</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:53:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81a7bf68-97c4-11f1-a9f5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Berita-Numbi-in-Mutekwatekwa-community-garden-in-Mutare-RFI-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe.jpg">© Farai Shawn Matiashe</source><dc:creator>Farai Shawn Matiashe</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Morocco arrests nearly 300 migrants near Ceuta amid renewed crossing fears</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260816-morocco-arrests-nearly-300-migrants-near-ceuta-amid-renewed-crossing-fears</link><description>
Scores of would-be migrants, most of them from sub-Saharan Africa, were intercepted in northern Morocco near the border with the Spanish exclave of Ceuta on Saturday, two weeks after tens of thousands of people attempted to enter the territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/565461a6-9731-11f1-9694-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215527124781.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/565461a6-9731-11f1-9694-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215527124781.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">796023ce-9957-11f1-bc95-7f396f569dcf</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:13:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/565461a6-9731-11f1-9694-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215527124781.jpg">AP Photo/Bernat Armangue - Bernat Armangue</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Algeria edge Morocco on penalties in WAFCON third-place play-off</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260816-algeria-edge-morocco-on-penalties-in-wafcon-third-place-play-off</link><description>
Morocco endured a second painful penalty shootout defeat in the space of four days as Algeria claimed third place at the Women’s Africa Cup of Nations on Saturday following a 1-1 draw in Rabat.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b8de40ee-98e9-11f1-899e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-08-15-at-22-41-10-L-Alg%C3%A9rie-s-offre-le-bronze-au-bout-du-suspense-face-au-Maroc.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b8de40ee-98e9-11f1-899e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-08-15-at-22-41-10-L-Alg%C3%A9rie-s-offre-le-bronze-au-bout-du-suspense-face-au-Maroc.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f95da7bc-98b8-11f1-aa82-e12dd09773c0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:26:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b8de40ee-98e9-11f1-899e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-08-15-at-22-41-10-L-Alg%C3%A9rie-s-offre-le-bronze-au-bout-du-suspense-face-au-Maroc.png">© Courtesy of CAF</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France probes unprecedented cyberattack after tax data of 678,000 users stolen</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260815-france-probes-unprecedented-cyberattack-after-tax-data-of-678-000-users-stolen</link><description>
French prosecutors have opened an investigation into a major cyberattack on the country’s tax administration that affected nearly 700,000 individuals and businesses, authorities said on Saturday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9f31b1d0-98b7-11f1-ac38-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/cyber-attack.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9f31b1d0-98b7-11f1-ac38-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/cyber-attack.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1ef8055a-98b7-11f1-8465-5f55dfe1c00c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 14:50:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9f31b1d0-98b7-11f1-ac38-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/cyber-attack.jpg">© Freepix</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Armenian Genocide survivors' grandson says 'political motives' block recognition</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260815-armenian-survivor-s-grandson-says-politics-still-blocks-genocide-recognition</link><description>
In 1915, the Ottoman Empire began the systematic deportation and massacre of its Armenian population. As many as 1.5 million Armenians were killed – widely regarded by historians as the twentieth century's first genocide, and the event for which the term was later coined. Stephan Pechdimaldji, the grandson of two of the survivors, spoke to RFI about why recognition still matters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">221a786c-969b-11f1-83af-a5d44a90634e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 19:03:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg">Getty Images via AFP - MARIO TAMA</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Nine killed in Israeli strikes on Lebanon as tensions test peace framework</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260815-nine-killed-in-israeli-strikes-on-lebanon-as-tensions-test-peace-framework</link><description>
At least nine people were killed in Israeli strikes on southern Lebanon on Saturday, according to Lebanon’s state news agency, in some of the deadliest attacks since Beirut agreed to a US-mediated framework aimed at ending the latest round of fighting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/498bb8d2-989b-11f1-a70f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Lebanon-Strike-bu-Israel.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/498bb8d2-989b-11f1-a70f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Lebanon-Strike-bu-Israel.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">70f27d30-989a-11f1-b0c2-51a8ef8c8f74</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:14:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/498bb8d2-989b-11f1-a70f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Lebanon-Strike-bu-Israel.jpg">© Mahmoud ZAYYAT / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Five years into Taliban rule, Afghanistan seeks to ease international isolation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260815-five-years-into-taliban-rule-afghanistan-seeks-to-ease-international-isolation</link><description>
In the five years since the Taliban seized back power in Afghanistan, the country's worsening human rights record has drawn sanctions and aid cuts. But despite refusing to officially recognise the fundamentalist movement's government, some countries are concluding that engaging with the Taliban has become unavoidable.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3a283ec-6be8-11f1-bfd3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26072483578608-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3a283ec-6be8-11f1-bfd3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26072483578608-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d87aa374-96f1-11f1-938b-1bb6596caa4b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 07:21:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3a283ec-6be8-11f1-bfd3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26072483578608-1.jpg">© AP - Hedayat Shah </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>In Turkey, one of the world's longest conflicts reaches a turning point</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260815-in-turkey-one-of-the-world-s-longest-conflicts-reaches-a-turning-point</link><description>
Turkey stands on the threshold of closing a conflict spanning almost 50 years, after the Turkish parliament this week passed a law allowing exiled Kurdish militants to return home and rejoin society. The legislation aims to end the war with the Kurdistan Workers' Party (PKK), which has battled the Turkish state for independence since 1984.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e4d800d6-f5ed-11ef-8568-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24155534800968.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e4d800d6-f5ed-11ef-8568-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24155534800968.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">050704c0-97e5-11f1-9f60-61ddff2f7428</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 10:52:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Law on assisted dying wins constitutional approval in France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260814-law-on-assisted-dying-wins-constitutional-approval-in-france</link><description>
France's Constitutional Council on Friday approved a law creating a right to assisted dying, removing the last major legal obstacle before the measure can be enacted and implemented.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3e3cd768-77a2-11ed-a3cf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_15M4NW.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3e3cd768-77a2-11ed-a3cf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_15M4NW.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">26163be6-97ee-11f1-94eb-8707596c334a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:11:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3e3cd768-77a2-11ed-a3cf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_15M4NW.jpg">© AFP - JEAN-CHRISTOPHE VERHAEGEN </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Fake accounts and false rumours drive new Ceuta crossing campaign</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260814-fake-accounts-and-false-rumours-drive-new-ceuta-crossing-campaign</link><description>
Calls for a new mass crossing into Ceuta, a Spanish enclave on Morocco's Mediterranean coast, have flooded Moroccan social media, with posts urging migrants to rush the border on Saturday. An RFI investigation found the campaign was fuelled by false rumours, suspicious accounts and signs of artificial amplification.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/74e6b070-972b-11f1-af60-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Ceuta-15-aout-Espagne-Maroc-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/74e6b070-972b-11f1-af60-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Ceuta-15-aout-Espagne-Maroc-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a3e28e4a-97f2-11f1-990a-af55d9f4e9ef</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:04:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/74e6b070-972b-11f1-af60-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Ceuta-15-aout-Espagne-Maroc-1.png">© Screengrabs compiled by RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>US missionary kidnapped in Niger freed after more than nine months</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260814-us-missionary-kidnapped-in-niger-freed-after-more-than-nine-months-in-captivity</link><description>
American Kevin Rideout, who worked as a pilot for an evangelical organisation, has been freed after he was kidnapped in October 2025 in Niamey. His release comes as the security situation remains tense in Niger. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2159fc1a-6c5a-11f1-b030-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-19T041459Z-311690609-RC2RWLA8S6JE-RTRMADP-3-NIGER-SECURITY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2159fc1a-6c5a-11f1-b030-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-19T041459Z-311690609-RC2RWLA8S6JE-RTRMADP-3-NIGER-SECURITY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aaa8747c-97e0-11f1-9d1b-61ddff2f7428</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:22:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2159fc1a-6c5a-11f1-b030-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-19T041459Z-311690609-RC2RWLA8S6JE-RTRMADP-3-NIGER-SECURITY.jpg">via REUTERS - ORTN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Top French court scraps social media ban for children under 15</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260814-top-french-court-scraps-social-media-ban-for-children-under-15</link><description>
France's Constitutional Council struck down a law on Friday that would have banned children under 15 from using social media from September. The judges ruled that the measure placed a disproportionate restriction on freedom of expression and communication.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/21dd94ca-97e4-11f1-8302-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25149163043530.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/21dd94ca-97e4-11f1-8302-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25149163043530.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">66562b0e-97e3-11f1-9c2d-3774d7b74ff3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 13:59:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/21dd94ca-97e4-11f1-8302-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25149163043530.jpg">© AP - Kiichiro Sato </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French firefighters threaten to strike over lack of resources</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260814-french-firefighters-threaten-to-strike-over-lack-of-resources</link><description>
As wildfires continue to burn across France, representatives of firefighters' unions said they would go on strike in September to protest a lack of resources. Despite a meeting with the interior minister on Thursday, they say they are unhappy with the government's response so far.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ed94ca0-8b72-11f1-8c21-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26209755840474.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ed94ca0-8b72-11f1-8c21-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26209755840474.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c3c773d2-97bc-11f1-ac7a-91dcbd8159e7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 11:39:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ed94ca0-8b72-11f1-8c21-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26209755840474.jpg">© AP Photo/Emma Da Silva</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Farage wins UK by-election as Count Binface claims 'moral victory'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260813-farage-wins-uk-by-election-as-count-binface-claims-moral-victory</link><description>
Hard-right British politician Nigel Farage reclaimed his seat in a by-election, according to the final tally Friday, though his main rival and joke candidate Count Binface took an larger than expected share of the ballot.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f50c945a-97ac-11f1-8012-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/78f883b2cf1f30f756558a7c5f4e0c7c88ce82bb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f50c945a-97ac-11f1-8012-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/78f883b2cf1f30f756558a7c5f4e0c7c88ce82bb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">592a3810-96be-11f1-9b66-8f0088c55881</guid><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 02:26:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f50c945a-97ac-11f1-8012-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/78f883b2cf1f30f756558a7c5f4e0c7c88ce82bb.jpg">© Henry NICHOLLS / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Zambia suspends vote counting nationwide citing violence</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260814-zambia-suspends-vote-counting-nationwide-citing-violence</link><description>
Zambia suspended vote counting nationwide on Friday following reports of violence in some districts, the electoral commission said.
